
  <sn><md>### Ecological and Environmental Impacts

| Impact | What happens | Possible result |
|---|---|---|
| `DNA damage` | Pollutants damage DNA directly or produce harmful molecules called reactive oxygen species. | Cells may not function or divide normally. |
| `Poor wildlife health` | Exposure can cause DNA and chromosome abnormalities and weaken immune systems. | Animals may become more vulnerable to disease. |
| `Reproductive problems` | DNA damage and hormone disruption can interfere with reproduction. | Animals may have fewer offspring or offspring with developmental abnormalities. |
| `Population decline` | Illness and reduced reproduction affect the number of organisms. | Wildlife populations may decrease. |
| `Loss of biodiversity` | Sensitive species may disappear from polluted areas. | Fewer species remain in the ecosystem. |
| `Tumors in wildlife` | Unrepaired DNA damage can cause cells to grow uncontrollably. | Tumors may develop and sometimes cause death. |

</md></sn>
